hi I'm Annie whoo and I'm a mathematics  teacher two years ago I started writing  this book where is wonderful world of  maths it's a cheesy title for a cheesy  person and what this book is about is  that when I was at school  loving the humanities and never really  appreciating mathematics is a subject I  came from that background and then as I  began preparing to be a mathematics  teacher and then started teaching it I  discovered all of these things about  mathematics that I had never known in  high school and I thought these are  amazing and surprising and beautiful and  these really gripped me and I thought if  people knew more about this if people  heard these melodies of mathematics they  may be able to come to a richer and  deeper appreciation of this subject so  things like how in nature you know a  bolt of lightning and the shape of a  river delta and the branches of a tree  and the capillaries that transport blood  around your body they all shared the  same geometry what is up with that and  the answer is fractal geometry is one of  most amazing things that students don't  learn very much about at school and if  they can sort of grab onto that and  realize that there are answers to the  questions like this but mathematics is a  sense that allows us to perceive the  world in a whole new way then they'll be  able to enjoy and appreciate it and  that's that's what this book is about  every chapter is a new thing that I  discovered that I thought I can't  believe I don't know this and I bet  others don't know her too I wonder if  they'd be interested in discovering it  as well
 

